MAME FM: the feedback and the DAC without shifting a negative number

Two more places where a signed value is scaled with a left shift, which is
undefined behaviour when it is negative. UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the
program at the first of them:

  src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c:1714:68: runtime error: left shift of
  negative value -12

* chan_calc() scales the feedback, the sum of the two previous outputs of
  operator 1, by the feedback shift. The shift is 0 or 7 to 13 and the sum
  stays within about 16384, so the product is well inside an int.

* The YM2612's DAC value is the byte of register 0x2A, centred on 0x80 and
  scaled by 64, in the two places that set it.

Multiplications say the same thing and are defined. The YM2612 and the
YM2608 cores share the feedback line; the DAC belongs to the YM2612 alone.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c b/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
index 4ac3de0..72ad38a 100644
--- a/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
+++ b/src/chips/mame/mame_ym2612fm.c
@@ -1711,7 +1711,7 @@ INLINE void chan_calc(YM2612 *F2612, FM_OPN *OPN, FM_CH *CH)
       if (!CH->FB)
         out=0;
 
-      CH->op1_out[1] = op_calc1(CH->SLOT[SLOT1].phase, eg_out, (out<<CH->FB) );
+      CH->op1_out[1] = op_calc1(CH->SLOT[SLOT1].phase, eg_out, (out * (1 << CH->FB)) );
     }
   }
 
@@ -2581,7 +2581,7 @@ void ym2612_postload(void *chip)
 		int r;
 
 		/* DAC data & port */
-		F2612->dacout = ((int)F2612->REGS[0x2a] - 0x80) << 6;	/* level unknown */
+		F2612->dacout = ((int)F2612->REGS[0x2a] - 0x80) * 64;	/* level unknown */
 		F2612->dacen  = F2612->REGS[0x2d] & 0x80;
 		/* OPN registers */
 		/* DT / MULTI , TL , KS / AR , AMON / DR , SR , SL / RR , SSG-EG */
@@ -2789,7 +2789,7 @@ int ym2612_write(void *chip, int a, UINT8 v)
 			{
 			case 0x2a:	/* DAC data (YM2612) */
 				ym2612_update_one(chip, DUMMYBUF, 0);
-				F2612->dacout = ((int)v - 0x80) << 6;	/* level unknown */
+				F2612->dacout = ((int)v - 0x80) * 64;	/* level unknown */
 				break;
 			case 0x2b:	/* DAC Sel  (YM2612) */
 				/* b7 = dac enable */
diff --git a/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp b/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
index 3fda9f1..e59160a 100644
--- a/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
+++ b/src/chips/mamefm/fm.cpp
@@ -1423,7 +1423,7 @@ static inline void chan_calc(FM_OPN *OPN, FM_CH *CH, int chnum)
 			if (!CH->FB)
 				out=0;
 
-			CH->op1_out[1] = op_calc1(CH->SLOT[SLOT1].phase, eg_out, (out<<CH->FB) );
+			CH->op1_out[1] = op_calc1(CH->SLOT[SLOT1].phase, eg_out, (out * (1 << CH->FB)) );
 		}
 	}
 
